# One turn pushes until the list has no room left and its elements move, and fills it. The pushes are written out: a loop that goes by the length would never end under the lie.
# The lie, testing=StorageAndLengthsAreTakenToBeAsInFront: the turns of a loop are taken to leave the storage of lists and of views, and so their lengths, as they were in front of it: what a turn reads of them is read once, in front. The last two turns read the elements where they lay: nothing has been collected since, and nothing is stored there.
# Under testing=TestsEveryPosition (--aot-harden=ignore-told-ranges) and testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime (--aot-harden=proof-checks) the same records are built at the same places, and what was read in front is held against the cell in the turn: the process stops by name.
